Certainly! Below is a complete Unity C# script for a custom EditorWindow named **SetSortingLayer**. When you open this window, you can select a sorting layer from a dropdown. Clicking the "Apply to Selected" button will then assign that sorting layer to all selected GameObjects in the Hierarchy, updating any components that use a `Renderer` (like `SpriteRenderer`, `MeshRenderer`, etc.) which have a `sortingLayerName` property.

### How to use:
1. Save this script in an `Editor` folder within your Unity project (e.g., `Assets/Editor/SetSortingLayer.cs`).
2. Open the window via **Window > Set Sorting Layer**.
3. Select the desired sorting layer from the dropdown.
4. Select one or more GameObjects in the Hierarchy.
5. Click **Apply to Selected**.

