Creating a custom After Effects panel and plugin that integrates with the ElevenLabs API involves several steps, including building a user interface, handling user input, making API requests, downloading audio files, and adding them to the timeline. Below is a comprehensive guide and example code snippets to help you develop this functionality.

---

## Overview

- **UI Panel**: Built with Adobe's CEP (Common Extensibility Platform) using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
- **API Integration**: Use JavaScript (ExtendScript or CEP scripts) to communicate with ElevenLabs API.
- **Features**:
  - Login with API key or credentials.
  - Select available voices.
  - Input text; press Enter to generate speech.
  - Download MP3 and add as a new audio layer.
  - "3x" option: send three concurrent requests, add one or three versions.

---

## Step 1: Set Up the CEP Panel

Create a folder structure:

```
MyElevenLabsAE/
├── manifest.xml
├── index.html
├── main.js
├── styles.css
```

### `manifest.xml`

Defines the CEP panel:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ExtensionManifest Version="7.0" ExtensionBundleId="com.yourdomain.elevenlabsae" ExtensionBundleVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://www.adobe.com/extension/manifest/7.0">
  <ExtensionList>
    <Extension Id="com.yourdomain.elevenlabsae.panel"/>
  </ExtensionList>
  <ExecutionEnvironment>
    <HostList>
      <Host Name="AEFT" Version="17.0"/>
    </HostList>
    <Locale>en_US</Locale>
    <ScriptPath>./main.js</ScriptPath>
  </ExecutionEnvironment>
  <DispatchInfo>
    <Resources>
      <MainPath>index.html</MainPath>
    </Resources>
  </DispatchInfo>
</ExtensionManifest>
```

---

## Step 2: Create the UI (`index.html`)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>ElevenLabs TTS for AE</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <h2>ElevenLabs TTS</h2>
  <div>
    <label for="apiKey">API Key:</label>
    <input type="password" id="apiKey" placeholder="Enter your API key" />
  </div>
  <div>
    <label for="voiceSelect">Voice:</label>
    <select id="voiceSelect">
      <option value="">Loading voices...</option>
    </select>
  </div>
  <div>
    <label for="textInput">Text:</label><br />
    <textarea id="textInput" rows="4" cols="50" placeholder="Type text and press Enter"></textarea>
  </div>
  <div>
    <label><input type="checkbox" id="multiview" /> 3x</label>
  </div>
  <button id="refreshVoices">Refresh Voices</button>
  <div id="status"></div>

  <script src="main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## Step 3: Style (`styles.css`)

```css
body {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  padding: 10px;
  width: 300px;
}

